Useful to know for those trying to acquire the Fish Disk sources for
porting to MS-Windows, the zip files accessible here:

http://gnuwin32.sourceforge.net/packages/lha.htm

contain tools to unpack the *.lha files, a common archive file for the
Amiga "back in the day" but very obscure today. Once unpacked,
running the lha.exe without any parameters gives a "how to use"
message.

xanthian, who for a while maintained the lha archiver source code,
in a form portable between the Amiga and MS-DOS.




